<title>INDIA: Indian silver falls on imported arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian silver falls on imported arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian silver prices fell in early trade on Friday with improved arrivals of imported silver triggering light profit-taking, dealers said.</p>
<p>Silver was steady on Thursday but was up by 50 rupees per kg on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Gold hand held steady in a narrow trading range amid limited activity. The trading focus remained on silver in early session trade while gold was less in demand.</p>
<p>Prices of a gold biscuit (116.50 grammes) remained steady at 58,700 rupees. They were down by 100 rupees on Thursday, but up by 200 rupees on Wednesday.  </p>
